{"uid":"5f16e5d804821686","name":"test_task_dialog_lists_the_iterations_behind_its_total","fullName":"tests.test_browser_hub#test_task_dialog_lists_the_iterations_behind_its_total","historyId":"79c7a870e7891629d63b434d5da0a7df","time":{"start":1791946308427,"stop":1791946313730,"duration":5303},"description":"Task 037 (G.5), inverted for task 001/PRD I.1 (#207/#29): the task\n    dialog opened from the tasks table lists the INDIVIDUAL iterations the\n    row's own timeDisplay/costDisplay total (task 036, G.4) was summed from\n    -- each with its tier and its own per-iteration cost -- bounded to\n    exactly the run's CURRENT approach's own two iterations against this\n    task, never a different task's, and never an EARLIER approach's own\n    same-numbered task attempt either.\n\n    Same three-iteration, approach-boundary fixture shape as\n    `test_task_table_shows_summed_time_and_cost_across_two_iterations`\n    above (task id `030`, a stale approach-1 attempt plus the current\n    approach 2's validation-failed-then-re-claim pair) PLUS a FOURTH\n    iteration, also in the current approach, dispatched against a\n    DIFFERENT task (`999`) -- so the breakdown proves it is bounded to BOTH\n    this approach AND this task: never the stale approach-1 iteration\n    (iteration #1, same task id, wrong approach) and never the approach-2\n    iteration against the unrelated task (#4, same approach, wrong task).\n\n    Against the pre-fix `task_totals` (bd94c695, before task 001/32044015\n    approach-namespaced the keys), this node fails: a flat `taskId`-only key\n    folds iteration #1's stale approach-1 entry into task \"030\"'s\n    breakdown, so `[b[\"number\"] for b in breakdown] == [2, 3]` below does\n    not hold (see the commit message for the captured failure).\n    ","descriptionHtml":"<p>Task 037 (G.5), inverted for task 001/PRD I.1 (#207/#29): the task<br />\ndialog opened from the tasks table lists the INDIVIDUAL iterations the<br />\nrow's own timeDisplay/costDisplay total (task 036, G.4) was summed from<br />\n-- each with its tier and its own per-iteration cost -- bounded to<br />\nexactly the run's CURRENT approach's own two iterations against this<br />\ntask, never a different task's, and never an EARLIER approach's own<br />\nsame-numbered task attempt either.</p>\n<pre><code>Same three-iteration, approach-boundary fixture shape as\n`test_task_table_shows_summed_time_and_cost_across_two_iterations`\nabove (task id `030`, a stale approach-1 attempt plus the current\napproach 2's validation-failed-then-re-claim pair) PLUS a FOURTH\niteration, also in the current approach, dispatched against a\nDIFFERENT task (`999`) -- so the breakdown proves it is bounded to BOTH\nthis approach AND this task: never the stale approach-1 iteration\n(iteration #1, same task id, wrong approach) and never the approach-2\niteration against the unrelated task (#4, same approach, wrong task).\n\nAgainst the pre-fix `task_totals` (bd94c695, before task 001/32044015\napproach-namespaced the keys), this node fails: a flat `taskId`-only key\nfolds iteration #1's stale approach-1 entry into task &quot;030&quot;'s\nbreakdown, so `[b[&quot;number&quot;] for b in breakdown] == [2, 3]` below does\nnot hold (see the commit message for the captured failure).\n</code></pre>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"event_loop_policy","time":{"start":1791945810103,"stop":1791945810103,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"tmp_path_factory","time":{"start":1791945810104,"stop":1791945810104,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_i